1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,500
Hello, judges.

2
00:00:01,920 --> 00:00:05,940
We are Team TARK, participating in Smart India Hackathon 2026.

3
00:00:06,600 --> 00:00:10,960
We present HYDROOVERITY, our proposed solution for smarter water

4
00:00:10,960 --> 00:00:13,700
pipeline leak detection and evidence-based maintenance.

5
00:00:14,289 --> 00:00:17,529
Every day, water moves through pipelines beneath our roads and homes.

6
00:00:18,309 --> 00:00:22,329
We notice it only when taps run dry, pressure drops or water appears where it

7
00:00:22,329 --> 00:00:22,669
should not.

8
00:00:23,469 --> 00:00:26,069
Now imagine a small leak at a buried pipe joint.

9
00:00:26,749 --> 00:00:27,989
It may stay hidden for days.

10
00:00:28,869 --> 00:00:32,409
Wet soil could be caused by rain, low pressure might come from tank filling

11
00:00:32,409 --> 00:00:33,289
or normal demand.

12
00:00:34,229 --> 00:00:38,029
And in areas where water arrives only during certain hours, detecting a leak

13
00:00:38,029 --> 00:00:39,249
becomes even more difficult.

14
00:00:39,909 --> 00:00:43,929
The challenge is interpreting the evidence, choosing where to investigate

15
00:00:43,929 --> 00:00:46,329
and confirming whether a repair worked.

16
00:00:47,309 --> 00:00:51,629
This is the problem behind HYDROOVERITY developed by Team TARK for Smart

17
00:00:51,629 --> 00:00:53,389
India Hackathon 2026.

18
00:00:54,289 --> 00:00:58,609
Our mission is simple, find the leak, understand the evidence, verify

19
00:00:58,609 --> 00:00:59,229
the repair.

20
00:01:00,269 --> 00:01:04,549
HYDROOVERITY brings together four connected ideas, HYDRO-WATCH, GUARD

21
00:01:04,549 --> 00:01:07,229
-5, HYDRO-EAR and HYDRO-VERIFY.

22
00:01:08,269 --> 00:01:11,489
Instead of trusting one sensor, it builds evidence step by step.

23
00:01:12,169 --> 00:01:14,429
First, HYDRO-WATCH looks at the bigger picture.

24
00:01:15,069 --> 00:01:18,889
Its proposed sensors measure pressure and available flow, while the software

25
00:01:18,889 --> 00:01:21,469
considers supply conditions and instrument quality.

26
00:01:22,149 --> 00:01:26,549
Is the pipeline off, filling, steady, draining, or is the state

27
00:01:26,549 --> 00:01:26,769
unknown?

28
00:01:27,669 --> 00:01:31,009
A suspicious water imbalance deserves attention, but it does not

29
00:01:31,009 --> 00:01:32,289
automatically prove a leak.

30
00:01:33,209 --> 00:01:36,649
Next comes our key mechanical design idea, GUARD-5.

31
00:01:37,189 --> 00:01:40,209
Picture a removable collar around an accessible pipe joint.

32
00:01:41,029 --> 00:01:44,429
Inside the proposed collar are three protected wetness collection paths,

33
00:01:45,069 --> 00:01:46,229
called A, B and C.

34
00:01:47,049 --> 00:01:51,289
A fourth channel, EXT, watches for environmental water, such as rain

35
00:01:51,289 --> 00:01:51,769
or splash.

36
00:01:52,769 --> 00:01:57,069
A fifth bypass, watches for water that escapes the intended collection paths.

37
00:01:58,029 --> 00:02:01,589
The aim is to ask not just whether water appeared, but where and why.

38
00:02:02,469 --> 00:02:06,029
This five-channel collector is digitally designed, but its real collection

39
00:02:06,029 --> 00:02:08,129
performance still needs physical testing.

40
00:02:09,089 --> 00:02:12,589
For suitable pipe sections, HYDRO-EAR adds another kind of evidence.

41
00:02:13,469 --> 00:02:15,669
Two contact pickups listen from different positions.

42
00:02:16,609 --> 00:02:20,489
A proposed stereo converter keeps both recordings on the same sampling clock,

43
00:02:20,909 --> 00:02:23,809
so timing differences can support a possible leak interval.

44
00:02:24,649 --> 00:02:28,349
If the signal is weak, the pressure is insufficient, or the pipe path is

45
00:02:28,349 --> 00:02:31,849
uncertain, the correct result may be no reliable location at all.

46
00:02:32,769 --> 00:02:36,529
Together, these ideas turn a vague alarm into a more careful investigation.

47
00:02:37,409 --> 00:02:39,229
But the next question matters just as much.

48
00:02:39,989 --> 00:02:42,149
Once a problem is reported, what happens next?

49
00:02:42,403 --> 00:02:43,643
Let us follow one example.

50
00:02:44,503 --> 00:02:48,103
The incident you are about to see is a simulated demonstration, not a leak

51
00:02:48,103 --> 00:02:49,223
found in a real village.

52
00:02:50,703 --> 00:02:55,063
A resident notices unusual water near a pipeline and opens the HYDROOVERITY

53
00:02:55,063 --> 00:02:55,303
website.

54
00:02:56,383 --> 00:03:00,203
They sign in, describe the issue and submit a report with a trackable

55
00:03:00,203 --> 00:03:00,483
reference.

56
00:03:01,523 --> 00:03:05,963
Their report becomes a concern for the utility to review, not automatic proof

57
00:03:05,963 --> 00:03:06,903
that a pipe has broken.

58
00:03:08,263 --> 00:03:12,263
On the supervisor's dashboard, authorized staff review the request, record

59
00:03:12,263 --> 00:03:15,623
decisions, and connect a legitimate investigation where appropriate.

60
00:03:16,623 --> 00:03:20,703
Residents see safe progress updates, while internal notes remain restricted

61
00:03:20,703 --> 00:03:22,003
to the people who need them.

62
00:03:22,863 --> 00:03:25,943
Now imagine the engineer opens the scientific workspace.

63
00:03:26,963 --> 00:03:30,943
HYDROOVERITY can import and replay saved simulation results from its

64
00:03:30,943 --> 00:03:33,243
hydraulic, wetness, and acoustic models.

65
00:03:34,503 --> 00:03:38,683
Charts show pressure, wetness patterns, missing data, and reasons for

66
00:03:38,683 --> 00:03:38,943
warnings.

67
00:03:40,103 --> 00:03:41,623
The screen clearly says simulation.

68
00:03:42,763 --> 00:03:46,103
These are research scenarios, not live readings from installed sensors.

69
00:03:47,103 --> 00:03:51,283
In our example, the available evidence points to a pipe section that deserves

70
00:03:51,283 --> 00:03:51,623
inspection.

71
00:03:52,743 --> 00:03:53,783
It guides an investigation.

72
00:03:54,543 --> 00:03:56,683
It does not reveal an exact underground hole.

73
00:03:57,843 --> 00:04:02,123
Next, the supervisor creates or links an authorized work order and

74
00:04:02,123 --> 00:04:03,283
selects a suitable technician.

75
00:04:04,223 --> 00:04:08,503
Scheduling checks configured shifts, skills, areas, and bookings.

76
00:04:09,363 --> 00:04:13,263
A resident may request a visit, but only supervisor confirmation reserves

77
00:04:13,263 --> 00:04:13,663
time.

78
00:04:14,583 --> 00:04:18,503
Database rules help prevent two confirmed appointments from taking the same

79
00:04:18,503 --> 00:04:19,343
technician's time.

80
00:04:20,523 --> 00:04:23,643
The technician opens their assigned work on a mobile-friendly screen.

81
00:04:24,663 --> 00:04:28,763
They can see the permitted task details, record investigation findings, and

82
00:04:28,763 --> 00:04:29,503
update the visit.

83
00:04:29,503 --> 00:04:33,783
In a future physical trial, a qualified worker could inspect

84
00:04:33,783 --> 00:04:36,343
the joint and repair the pipe under approved procedures.

85
00:04:37,623 --> 00:04:41,243
HYDROOVERITY does not operate the valves or perform the repair itself.

86
00:04:42,583 --> 00:04:44,663
And this is where HYDRO-VERIFY becomes important.

87
00:04:45,843 --> 00:04:48,643
A completed visit is not the same as a completed repair.

88
00:04:49,503 --> 00:04:53,363
A repair record is not the same as proof that water loss has stopped.

89
00:04:54,323 --> 00:04:57,983
Reliable verification needs suitable before and after measurements, with

90
00:04:57,983 --> 00:05:00,583
comparable operating conditions and valid instruments.

91
00:05:01,763 --> 00:05:05,843
Our scientific simulations explore three possible conclusions – passed,

92
00:05:06,383 --> 00:05:07,943
failed, and not verifiable.

93
00:05:08,963 --> 00:05:12,763
But in the current operational software, a manual repair record without

94
00:05:12,763 --> 00:05:15,483
enough measured evidence remains not verifiable.

95
00:05:16,623 --> 00:05:18,383
The system must not invent success.

96
00:05:19,403 --> 00:05:23,203
Residents can track safe updates, receive in-app notifications,

97
00:05:24,123 --> 00:05:27,443
mark them read, and leave feedback after eligible case closure.

98
00:05:28,603 --> 00:05:32,663
A satisfaction rating can help improve service, but it cannot prove that a

99
00:05:32,663 --> 00:05:33,383
leak was fixed.

100
00:05:34,843 --> 00:05:38,403
From the first report to the final review, the objective is accountability.

101
00:05:39,643 --> 00:05:43,623
The right information, the right people, and evidence that stays attached to

102
00:05:43,623 --> 00:05:44,183
each decision.

103
00:05:44,529 --> 00:05:48,729
So, what makes HYDROOVERITY different from a basic leak alarm or

104
00:05:48,729 --> 00:05:49,629
complaint website?

105
00:05:50,509 --> 00:05:54,369
A pressure alarm detects change, a wetness pad senses contact.

106
00:05:55,049 --> 00:05:59,189
Acoustic methods may suggest a location, complaint portals collect reports.

107
00:06:00,109 --> 00:06:02,229
Each is useful, but each has limits.

108
00:06:03,849 --> 00:06:07,209
Our proposed approach connects these different clues to one accountable

109
00:06:07,209 --> 00:06:08,309
maintenance process.

110
00:06:08,909 --> 00:06:12,309
HYDRO-WATCH asks whether the supply conditions make an alarm meaningful.

111
00:06:12,849 --> 00:06:16,829
GUARD-5 is designed to observe five distinct water paths at an accessible

112
00:06:16,829 --> 00:06:17,269
joint.

113
00:06:17,829 --> 00:06:21,649
HYDRO-EAR gives a bounded acoustic candidate where the physics supports it.

114
00:06:22,069 --> 00:06:26,009
HYDRO-VERIFY asks whether there is enough evidence to trust the outcome of a

115
00:06:26,009 --> 00:06:26,249
repair.

116
00:06:26,809 --> 00:06:30,909
Our testable idea is better qualified decisions, with a complete trail from

117
00:06:30,909 --> 00:06:31,909
concern to review.

118
00:06:32,669 --> 00:06:36,289
We are not claiming to have invented leak detection, or to have proven that

119
00:06:36,289 --> 00:06:38,169
our collar outperforms existing sensors.

120
00:06:38,849 --> 00:06:41,929
In fact, our own simulated results reveal important weaknesses.

121
00:06:42,829 --> 00:06:46,889
In one nominal GUARD-5 comparison, simpler reference sensors performed better

122
00:06:46,889 --> 00:06:47,749
on the chosen benchmark.

123
00:06:48,529 --> 00:06:51,869
And some acoustic estimates were confidently wrong, even when the model

124
00:06:51,869 --> 00:06:52,649
accepted them.

125
00:06:53,849 --> 00:06:56,629
Rather than hiding those results, we preserved them.

126
00:06:57,049 --> 00:07:00,649
That tells us exactly what future physical experiments must challenge.

127
00:07:01,209 --> 00:07:05,049
Our private development software already supports resident reports, staff

128
00:07:05,049 --> 00:07:09,409
investigation, scheduling, notifications, feedback, scientific replay,

129
00:07:09,789 --> 00:07:11,749
access controls, and audit history.

130
00:07:12,169 --> 00:07:16,469
At the current reviewed baseline, it has 119 registered API operations

131
00:07:16,469 --> 00:07:19,249
and 57 migrated application tables.

132
00:07:19,569 --> 00:07:23,549
Automated integration and browser tests pass, but that does not turn

133
00:07:23,549 --> 00:07:25,849
simulated sensor evidence into field validation.

134
00:07:26,569 --> 00:07:28,509
The hardware is also designed digitally.

135
00:07:29,169 --> 00:07:32,469
Our proposed demonstration rig contains a supply and return pipe loop,

136
00:07:32,809 --> 00:07:36,949
controlled leak points, pressure and flow instrumentation, a removable GUARD

137
00:07:36,949 --> 00:07:39,569
-5 collar, and a portable paired acoustic setup.

138
00:07:40,089 --> 00:07:43,829
Its engineering files include parametric CAD, electronic connectivity drafts,

139
00:07:44,329 --> 00:07:45,229
and a materials list.

140
00:07:45,749 --> 00:07:50,249
The estimated complete prototype budget is 59,870 rupees

141
00:07:50,249 --> 00:07:52,389
against a 60,000 rupee planning ceiling.

142
00:07:52,929 --> 00:07:55,069
Actual supplier prices could exceed the ceiling.

143
00:07:55,929 --> 00:07:57,429
Affordability remains a goal.

144
00:07:58,129 --> 00:08:02,089
Physical tests must still cover wetness collection, rain, blockage,

145
00:08:02,409 --> 00:08:06,809
calibration, acoustic audibility, clock timing, electrical safety,

146
00:08:07,209 --> 00:08:08,109
and repair measurements.

147
00:08:08,889 --> 00:08:12,949
Privacy, offline operation, secure uploads, and public deployment

148
00:08:12,949 --> 00:08:15,029
also have remaining approval gates.

149
00:08:15,769 --> 00:08:19,769
So, HYDROOVERITY is not a claim that every water leak has already been

150
00:08:19,769 --> 00:08:20,049
solved.

151
00:08:20,749 --> 00:08:24,909
It is a working software platform, a reproducible scientific investigation

152
00:08:24,909 --> 00:08:29,329
and a physically unvalidated hardware design brought together around

153
00:08:29,329 --> 00:08:30,649
one practical question.

154
00:08:31,389 --> 00:08:35,529
When water is lost, can we move beyond suspicion, take responsible

155
00:08:35,529 --> 00:08:38,589
action, and know what the evidence really proves?

156
00:08:39,549 --> 00:08:40,249
HYDROOVERITY.

157
00:08:41,029 --> 00:08:44,349
Find the leak, understand the evidence, verify the repair.
